[h1]Detailed Map Tacks Fixes by Najane[/h1]

An [b]add-on[/b] for [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3507297712][b]Detailed Map Tacks[/b] by wltk[/url]. It fixes bugs and rough edges in that mod.

[b]It is not a replacement and it does nothing on its own.[/b] Detailed Map Tacks is required, and this mod declares it as a hard dependency - if that mod is missing or switched off, this one quietly does not apply rather than filling your log with errors.

[h2]What it fixes[/h2]
Nothing yet - this first version is the groundwork. Fixes will be listed here and in the change notes as they land, each one naming the problem in the host mod so you can tell when it has been fixed upstream.

[h2]Options[/h2]
Under [b]Options - Mods - Detailed Map Tacks Fixes by Najane[/b]:
[list]
[*] [b]Apply Detailed Map Tacks fixes[/b] (on by default) - turns every fix off without uninstalling the mod. This is the first thing to try if map tacks start misbehaving after a Detailed Map Tacks update.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]UI only.[/b] No rules, values or balance are changed. It does not affect saved games and can be removed mid-save.
[*] Loads after Detailed Map Tacks by design, and patches what is running rather than replacing any of its files - so it does not fight other map tack mods any more than they already fight each other.
[/list]

[h2]Reporting a problem[/h2]
Say which version of [b]both[/b] mods you have and attach [b]UI.log[/b]. Lines from this mod are tagged [b][najane-map-tacks][/b]. If switching the option above off makes the problem go away, that is the single most useful thing you can tell me.

[h2]Credits[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Detailed Map Tacks[/b] is by [b]wltk[/b]. This mod patches it - it does not include, fork or redistribute it. All credit for map tacks in Civilization VII goes there.
[*] Fixes by [b]Najane[/b].
[/list]
